#!/usr/bin/python3
"""hearth-server-apps: Settings › Home server › Server apps and Phone notifications (docs/SERVER-APPS.md).

The Server apps catalog: one-click game servers (Minecraft, Valheim, Terraria, Palworld) and self-hosted apps
(Vaultwarden, Immich, Navidrome, ntfy). Every one is off and not installed until you ask. Each runs in your own
rootless Podman as your own user service (hearth-app@<id>.service, systemd --user, no [Install]; its timer starts it
a minute after you sign in and is enabled only while it's on). Nothing here is part of starting the PC, the session,
Game Mode or Steam: a broken app only stops that app (it's tried 4 times in 15 minutes, then left stopped and you're
told). Images are pulled only when you press Install, then run with --pull=never. Your data lives in
~/Server apps/<name>, kept when an app is removed unless you confirm twice.

Phone notifications: Home server alerts and server apps that stopped, sent to the ntfy app on your phone (ntfy.sh or
your own ntfy server, also in the catalog), off until you turn it on. A user timer (hearth-server-ntfy.timer, only while
it's on) checks every 5 minutes.

Your choices: ~/.config/nimbus/server-apps.json through hearth_settings_io (atomic, .bak, merge under a lock; only the
key you changed is written; defaults are filled in when it's read, never saved). Install state:
~/.local/state/nimbus/server-apps.json. Passwords: ~/.local/state/nimbus/server-apps-secrets.json (0600), never in
settings, handed to Podman in a 0600 env file in your runtime folder (never on a command line).

  hearth-server-apps list                    JSON: the catalog with installed, on, running, reach, addresses, options
  hearth-server-apps quick                   the apps that are on, in short (Server mode's dashboard, Hearth Link)
  hearth-server-apps install ID | update ID  pull its images (in its own transient unit of yours, at low priority)
  hearth-server-apps set ID on|off           on needs it installed (and Minecraft's EULA accepted)
  hearth-server-apps set ID reach home|tailscale
  hearth-server-apps set ID eula on|off      Minecraft only
  hearth-server-apps opt ID KEY VALUE        its options (checked against the catalog's choices)
  hearth-server-apps password ID             its password on stdin (HEARTH_INPUT); empty clears it
  hearth-server-apps logs ID                 the last lines it printed
  hearth-server-apps remove ID [data sure really-sure]   its images go; its data only with both confirmations
  hearth-server-apps run ID | stop ID        what hearth-app@ID.service runs (ExecStart / ExecStop)
  hearth-server-apps job ID                  the install itself (started by install/update)
  hearth-server-apps ntfy                    phone notifications: settings and the last result
  hearth-server-apps ntfy-set KEY VALUE      on|alerts|apps (on|off); server URL; topic TOPIC|new
  hearth-server-apps ntfy-test               send a test notification now
  hearth-server-apps ntfy-forward            what hearth-server-ntfy.service runs: send what's new
Output: one JSON line; failures print "error: ..." and exit 1.
"""
